---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
const lang = 'en';
---

<DocsLayout lang={lang}>
  <h1 class="font-mono text-3xl font-bold text-mono-50">Getting Started</h1>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 text-sm text-mono-400">
    <li>Rust 1.75+ (for building runtime and CLI)</li>
    <li><code class="text-mono-200">protoc</code> &mdash; Protocol Buffers compiler</li>
    <li>Node.js 18+ (for web client development)</li>
    <li>Windows 10+ or Linux/macOS</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">1. Clone the Repositories</h2>
  <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/50 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-mono-300"><code>git clone https://github.com/RoamyDev/roamy-protocol.git
git clone https://github.com/RoamyDev/roamy-runtime.git
git clone https://github.com/RoamyDev/roamy-web.git</code></pre>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mono-400">
    Place them as sibling directories so <code class="text-mono-200">roamy-runtime</code> can find <code class="text-mono-200">roamy-protocol</code> via the workspace <code class="text-mono-200">path</code> dependency.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">2. Build and Run sessiond</h2>
  <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/50 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-mono-300"><code># Set protoc path (example)
export PROTOC="/usr/local/bin/protoc"   # Linux/macOS
$env:PROTOC = "C:\protoc\bin\protoc.exe"  # Windows PowerShell

# Build
cd roamy-runtime
cargo build

# Run the session daemon (interactive mode)
cargo run --bin sessiond</code></pre>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mono-400">
    When started interactively, sessiond prints a QR code pairing block in the terminal showing the connection URL, port, token, and QR code for mobile/web clients.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">3. Connect with the Web Client</h2>
  <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/50 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-mono-300"><code>cd ../roamy-web

# Regenerate Protobuf bindings (optional, if proto files changed)
npm run proto

# Start dev server
npm run dev</code></pre>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mono-400">
    Open <code class="text-mono-200">http://localhost:3000</code> in your browser, enter the WebSocket URL displayed by sessiond (e.g. <code class="text-mono-200">ws://127.0.0.1:9800</code>), and click <strong class="text-mono-200">Connect</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">4. (Optional) Use the CLI</h2>
  <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/50 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-mono-300"><code># Build the CLI binary
cargo build --bin roamy

# Start the daemon in background
roamy daemon start

# Launch a shell session
roamy shell

# List sessions
roamy list

# Reattach to a session
roamy join &lt;session-id&gt;</code></pre>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mono-400">
    Detach from a session with <kbd class="rounded border border-mono-700 bg-mono-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs text-mono-300">Ctrl+]</kbd> then <kbd class="rounded border border-mono-700 bg-mono-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs text-mono-300">d</kbd>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">5. Embedded Web Assets</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mono-400">
    To embed the web client directly into sessiond (single binary distribution), build with the <code class="text-mono-200">embed-web</code> feature:
  </p>
  <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/50 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-mono-300"><code># Build roamy-web first
cd roamy-web && npm run build

# Copy dist into sessiond's expected location, then build with feature
cargo build --bin sessiond --features embed-web</code></pre>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mono-400">
    sessiond will serve the embedded web assets on the HTTP port, so you don't need a separate web server.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
